rnalist do?\nIn Scenario 1, the journalist does filmmaking.\nIn Scenario 2, the journalist does thriller.\nAgain, we have two possibilities.\n\n3. What is the job of the person who watches adventure?\nIn Scenario 1, the person who watches adventure is a filmmaker.\nIn Scenario 2, the person who watches adventure is a police-officer.\n\n4. What is the job of the person who watches thriller?\nIn Scenario 1, the person who watches thriller is a journalist.\nIn Scenario 2, the person who watches thriller is a journalist.\n\nLet's revisit the constraints.\nWe know that the person who is a journalist is to the right of the person who watches adventure. This implies that the person who watches adventure must be in position 1. Then the journalist is in position 2.\nP1: Adventure, Hobby1\nP2: Journalist, Hobby2\n\nSince the police-officer is not the same as the person who likes filmmaking, and the person who is a journalist is in position 2, the person who likes filmmaking must be in position 1.\nP1: Adventure, Filmmaking\nP2: Journalist, Thriller\n\nSo the person who watches adventure is in position 1.\nThe hobby of the person who is a journalist is filmmaking.\nThe job of the person who watches adventure is adventure.\nThe job of the person who watches thriller is journalist.\n\nFinal answer: 1, filmmaking, adventure, journalist</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.00201534666121006}, {"token": "'", "logprob": -0.004649304784834385}, {"token": "s", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁analyze", "logprob": -0.3462364375591278}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -1.9430925021879375e-05}, {"token": "▁given", "logprob": -0.14039145410060883}, {"token": "▁information", "logprob": -0.00023803261865396053}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.7501723170280457}, {"token": "\n", "logprob": -0.8142693042755127}, {"token": "Let", "logprob": -0.222984179854393}, {"token": "▁P", "logprob": -0.185431107878685}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "▁be", "logpro